      "number": 12,
      "reference": "Romans 8:38–39",
      "verse": "For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, nor things to come, Nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.",
      "explanation": "Paul declares that nothing in creation can separate believers from God's love in Christ. This is a reminder that God's love is not fragile or temporary. Even when our relationships change, circumstances shift or loneliness makes us feel disconnected, His love remains steadfast.",
      "letter": "My Kuchuuu,\n\nI hope you never confuse a quiet day with a forgotten heart.\n\nSometimes people become busy. Sometimes conversations become shorter. Sometimes distance makes things feel a little different.\n\nBut please don't let every silence convince you that love has disappeared.\n\nI want you to remember that God's love isn't measured by how many messages you receive or how many people are physically around you. His love is deeper and steadier than that.\n\nAnd when it comes to us, I want to keep showing you love through consistency. Not just beautiful words on beautiful days, but genuine effort in ordinary ones, too.\n\nYou deserve to feel secure in the relationships you hold close.\n\nI hope your heart always finds reasons to feel loved, my girl.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
