      "number": 13,
      "reference": "Psalm 9:9–10",
      "verse": "The LORD also will be a refuge for the oppressed, a refuge in times of trouble. And they that know thy name will put their trust in thee: for thou, LORD, hast not forsaken them that seek thee.",
      "explanation": "These verses describe God as a refuge for people facing trouble and oppression. A refuge is a place of safety when the outside world feels difficult. The passage reassures us that those who seek God are not forsaken, even when they are going through lonely or painful seasons.",
      "letter": "My sweetest Kuchuuu,\n\nI hope you always have somewhere your heart can rest.\n\nSomewhere you don't have to explain why you're quiet, why you're tired or why you don't feel like talking. Somewhere you can simply exist without feeling judged.\n\nI pray that God becomes that refuge for you whenever the world feels too loud.\n\nAnd I hope you build relationships that feel safe, too. Relationships where you can be honest without fearing that every little vulnerability will be used against you.\n\nYou don't need to pretend to be a different person to be accepted.\n\nI want you to feel comfortable being yourself with me. Even when you're not talkative, even when you're a little moody, even when all you need is some quiet affection.\n\nYou have a place in my heart, my girl.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
