      "number": 14,
      "reference": "Isaiah 41:13",
      "verse": "For I the LORD thy God will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee.",
      "explanation": "God describes Himself as holding His people's hand and reassuring them that He will help them. The image is intimate and comforting: not simply watching from a distance, but offering support and guidance. For someone feeling lonely, it reminds them that they do not have to face every difficult step unsupported.",
      "letter": "My little one,\n\nIf I could give you one thing for the days when loneliness feels especially heavy, it would be the feeling that you don't have to figure out everything by yourself.\n\nI hope you remember that asking for help doesn't make you weak. Reaching out doesn't make you needy. Missing someone doesn't make you foolish.\n\nSometimes we simply need a hand to hold, a familiar voice or a little reassurance that things will be okay.\n\nAnd I hope you never stop asking God for that comfort.\n\nWhen you need me, please reach out. Don't sit there wondering whether you're disturbing me or whether your feelings are important enough to share.\n\nI want to make time for the little things that matter to you, too.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
