      "explanation": "These verses remind us to listen before reacting and to think before speaking. Anger can make us respond before we fully understand a situation. James teaches that uncontrolled anger does not produce the goodness God desires. Taking time to listen and calm ourselves can prevent words and actions we might later regret.",
      "letter": "My Kuchuuu,\n\nI know that sometimes things can get so frustrating that you just want to say everything that’s sitting inside your heart.\n\nAnd honestly, I don’t want you to feel that you must swallow every emotion just to keep the peace. If something hurts you, you should be able to say it.\n\nBut please, give yourself a little moment before responding when you’re angry. Not every thought needs to become a sentence, and not every feeling needs an immediate reaction.\n\nListen, breathe and let your heart settle a little. You can still stand up for yourself without hurting yourself or somebody else in the process.\n\nYour feelings deserve to be heard, my love. Just don’t let one angry moment speak for your entire heart.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
