      "number": 9,
      "reference": "Romans 12:19–21",
      "verse": "Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, saith the Lord. Therefore if thine enemy hunger, feed him; if he thirst, give him drink: for in so doing thou shalt heap coals of fire on his head. Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.",
      "explanation": "Paul teaches that revenge should not become our responsibility. Instead of returning harm for harm, we are encouraged to overcome evil with good. This does not mean accepting mistreatment or ignoring justice. It means refusing to let hatred and revenge take control of our actions.",
      "letter": "My sweetest girl,\n\nI hope nobody ever convinces you that being kind means being weak.\n\nYou can forgive someone without allowing them to repeat the same hurt. You can wish someone well from a distance. You can choose not to take revenge while still deciding that a relationship is no longer healthy for you.\n\nPlease remember that kindness doesn’t require you to abandon your boundaries.\n\nI don’t want you to spend your precious time planning how to make someone regret hurting you. Your life has so much more to offer than that.\n\nLet God handle what you cannot change. Keep your dignity, protect your heart and continue being the person you want to be.\n\nDon’t let somebody else’s darkness take away your light, Kuchuuu.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
