      "reference": "Matthew 5:9",
      "verse": "Blessed are the peacemakers: for they shall be called the children of God.",
      "explanation": "Jesus calls peacemakers blessed. A peacemaker is not someone who avoids every disagreement or remains silent when something is wrong. Rather, a peacemaker seeks understanding, fairness and reconciliation wherever possible. This verse encourages us to contribute to peace instead of feeding unnecessary conflict.",
      "letter": "My little peace-maker,\n\nI hope you never feel that every disagreement has to become a battle.\n\nSometimes people simply see things differently. Sometimes misunderstandings happen, and sometimes two people need to sit down and listen to each other.\n\nI hope you always have the courage to choose a conversation over unnecessary arguments.\n\nBut please remember, keeping peace doesn’t mean keeping quiet about something that hurts you. Your voice matters, too.\n\nI want you to have relationships where both people make an effort to understand one another, where apologies are genuine and where peace isn’t maintained by just one person making all the sacrifices.\n\nYou deserve that kind of peace, my love.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
