      "reference": "Proverbs 12:16",
      "verse": "A fool’s wrath is presently known: but a prudent man covereth shame.",
      "explanation": "This proverb contrasts an impulsive display of anger with the restraint of a thoughtful person. It encourages us not to let every irritation immediately become an outward reaction. Being prudent means recognising that we have a choice about how we respond, even when something has upset us.",
      "letter": "My Gulaabiiii,\n\nI hope you never feel that you have to show everybody exactly how angry you are for them to understand that something matters to you.\n\nSometimes a little pause says more than a hundred angry words.\n\nYou can tell someone that you’re upset without raising your voice. You can explain what hurt you without losing your composure. And you can walk away from a conversation until you’re ready to speak properly.\n\nI want you to feel confident in your emotions, not frightened of them.\n\nYour feelings are important, my girl. Just remember that you have the power to choose how you express them.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
