      "verse": "A fool uttereth all his mind: but a wise man keepeth it in till afterwards.",
      "explanation": "This proverb warns against expressing every thought impulsively. When emotions are intense, we may say things that are exaggerated, unfair or unnecessarily hurtful. Wisdom sometimes means waiting until we are calmer before deciding what truly needs to be said.",
      "letter": "My little one,\n\nI know that when something upsets you, you might feel like saying everything at once.\n\nEvery thought, every complaint, every little thing that has been building up inside you.\n\nAnd sometimes expressing those feelings is exactly what you need. But I hope you give yourself a moment to separate what you genuinely want to communicate from what anger is making you say.\n\nYou don’t have to send that message immediately. You don’t have to finish that argument tonight.\n\nWrite your thoughts down if you need to. Take a little walk. Give your heart time to settle.\n\nThen speak when you can express yourself in a way that truly represents you.\n\nI hope your words always reflect your wisdom, my love.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
