      "reference": "James 3:17–18",
      "verse": "But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy. And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace.",
      "explanation": "James describes godly wisdom through qualities such as gentleness, mercy, fairness and peace. This passage reminds us that wisdom is not merely about knowing what to say; it is also about the spirit in which we say it. A peaceful heart seeks what is right without becoming cruel or unfair.",
      "letter": "My sweetest Kuchuuu,\n\nI hope you never lose your gentleness while learning how to protect yourself.\n\nI want you to be able to say no without feeling guilty, to disagree without becoming cruel and to stand your ground without losing your kindness.\n\nYou don’t need to become harsh to be taken seriously.\n\nAnd whenever you feel confused about how to respond to someone, I hope you ask God for wisdom before allowing anger to decide for you.\n\nMay you always have the courage to choose what is right, even when it is difficult.\n\nI love your soft heart, my girl. Please don’t let difficult people convince you that you must stop being kind.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
