      "explanation": "Paul describes love as patient, kind and not easily provoked. This passage reminds us that genuine love is not simply an emotion we express when everything is going well. It also appears in the way we treat one another during disagreements, disappointments and difficult moments. Love seeks understanding rather than unnecessary conflict.",
      "letter": "My Gulaabiiii,\n\nI hope we always remember that loving someone doesn’t mean we’ll never disagree.\n\nThere might be days when we misunderstand each other, when one of us gets irritated or when something doesn’t go the way we expected.\n\nBut I want us to remember that we’re on the same side.\n\nI don’t want us to turn every disagreement into a competition about who is right. I want us to listen, understand, apologise when needed and make an effort to do better.\n\nAnd I want you to know that you can tell me when something I do hurts you. I want to understand your feelings, not dismiss them.\n\nLove should give us a reason to become more patient with each other, not a reason to stop trying.\n\nLet’s keep choosing kindness, even on the days when it takes a little more effort.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
