      "explanation": "David speaks to his own soul, reminding himself not to forget God’s goodness. He remembers forgiveness, mercy, healing, protection and provision. This passage teaches us to look back at the many ways God has cared for us instead of allowing our attention to rest only on what is missing.",
      "letter": "My sweetest Kuchuuu,\n\nI want you to remember something whenever life makes you feel as though you have very little to be thankful for.\n\nLook back, my love.\n\nLook at the things you once worried about that eventually became okay. Remember the moments you thought you wouldn’t get through, yet here you are. Remember the forgiveness, the kindness, the unexpected help and the little joys that found their way into your life.\n\nSometimes we become so focused on what we still want that we forget how much has already been placed in our hands.\n\nAnd even when you cannot see everything God is doing, don’t forget what He has already done.\n\nI hope you never stop counting your blessings, even the quiet ones.\n\nYour Kishmish ♡"
